From 3d6a4a51bb67a404ba8c470b0bf4b7708d12df09 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 02:12:30 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(boundary): separate inside and outside boundary
 offsets

The one Boundary offset moved both lines of an open boundary: the line
that the user picked and the stock side. A negative value to cut less
air also moved the picked edge. AreaControls gets outer_offset for the
outer line; offset now moves only the picked line (or the whole closed
area). Equal values run the old law exactly. An old project file loads
its one offset into both and saves the same bytes. The Boundary group
shows two rows, and set_operation_area takes outer_offset.

Fixes #3338

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
